WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:11.893
In tutorial 11.2, you'll hand audit findings
and recommendations to your developers,

00:00:11.943 --> 00:00:15.020
as tickets in Jira, Linear or Asana.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:20.677
First, open Company settings, choose
Integrations, and find Issue trackers.

00:00:22.001 --> 00:00:26.681
Click Connect beside your tracker.
For Linear, paste a personal API key,

00:00:26.731 --> 00:00:27.844
and your team key.

00:00:29.051 --> 00:00:33.126
Not sure where to find the key? The guide
button beside each tracker shows you,

00:00:33.176 --> 00:00:34.302
step by step.

00:00:35.526 --> 00:00:41.171
For Jira, add your Jira address, your account
e-mail, an API token, the project key,

00:00:41.221 --> 00:00:42.309
and the issue type.

00:00:43.505 --> 00:00:47.680
Then click Check and connect. The token
is checked with your tracker first,

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.272
and it shows as Connected.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:55.918
Now open Technical health. Every open
finding has a Create ticket button.

00:00:57.505 --> 00:01:00.005
Your recommendations have the same button,

00:01:00.055 --> 00:01:02.653
so any next step can go
to your developers too.

00:01:04.005 --> 00:01:07.255
Click Create ticket, and the
finding goes to your tracker,

00:01:07.305 --> 00:01:09.068
with its evidence and the fix.

00:01:11.005 --> 00:01:15.105
Once it's made, the button shows the ticket
number and its status in your tracker,

00:01:15.155 --> 00:01:16.366
like In progress.

00:01:18.551 --> 00:01:22.051
And under Issue trackers, you can
see how many tickets were made,

00:01:22.101 --> 00:01:23.418
and how many are done.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:29.355
So, connect your issue tracker,
open a finding or recommendation,

00:01:29.405 --> 00:01:31.960
then create a ticket
and follow its status.

00:01:32.963 --> 00:01:39.370
Your findings now reach your developers.
Next, export your data, in tutorial 11.3.
